ication, (concretely) ornament","p":"gah-av-aw'","t":"gaavah","g":"pride","fb":[],"v":[5836,5839,13902,14042,14348,14353,14448,14616,14933,15025,16774,17246,17837,17908,17916,17974,18128,20108,22830]},"H1391":{"l":"גִּבְעוֹן","x":"Gibʻôwn","d":"Gibon, a place in Palestine","p":"ghib-ohn'","t":"gibon","g":"Gibeon","fb":[["gibeon","Gibeon","","They tricked Joshua into a treaty by dressing as travellers from far away, the Hivites of this city northwest of Jerusalem, and so they lived but served at Israel's sanctuary. The tabernacle stood at Gibeon for years, and Solomon had his dream there. At el-Jib dozens of jar handles stamped with the name have settled where it was.","place",33]],"v":[6040,6054,6065,6066,6068,6069,6070,6074,6076,6105,6126,6318,6398,8061,8062,8065,8073,8111,8562,8820,8821,9053,10604,10604,10650,10650,10790,10859,10963,11197,11207,12334,12445,18184,19618,19968,19972]},"H1382":{"l":"גִּבְלִי","x":"Giblîy","d":"a Gebalite, or inhabitant of Gebal","p":"ghib-lee'","t":"gibli","g":"Gebalites","fb":[],"v":[6159,8896]},"H1390":{"l":"גִּבְעָה","x":"Gibʻâh","d":"Gibah; the name of three places in Palestine","p":"ghib-aw'","t":"gibah","g":"Gibeah","fb":[],"v":[6259,6321,7036,7037,7038,7039,7040,7058,7059,7063,7067,7068,7069,7073,7074,7075,7079,7083,7084,7085,7088,7090,7091,7097,7444,7449,7487,7500,7510,7524,7594,7793,7829,7906,8586,8682,10704,11455,17878,22159,22216,22233,22233]},"H1387":{"l":"גֶּבַע","x":"Gebaʻ","d":"Geba, a place in Palestine","p":"gheh'-bah","t":"geba","g":"Geba","fb":[["gaba","Gaba","Geba","Another English spelling of Geba, a Levitical city in Benjamin by the pass of Michmash. Jonathan raided a Philistine garrison there, and later it marked the line between the northern and southern kingdoms.","place",16],["gaba-2","Gaba","Gibeah","Named once, in Judges, and nowhere else.","place",1],["gaba-3","Gaba","Gibeon","Named once, in 2 Samuel, and nowhere else.","place",1],["gaba-4","Gaba","Maareh-geba","Judges names him once, and nothing else is recorded.","place",1]],"v":[6317,6398,7064,7087,7488,7501,7513,8157,9271,10173,10514,10581,11515,12053,12450,12618,12652,17878,23077]},"H1329":{"l":"בְּתוּל","x":"Bᵉthûwl","d":"Bethul (i.e. Bethuel), a place in Palestine","p":"beth-ool'","t":"bethul","g":"Bethul","fb":[["bethuel-2","Bethuel","Bethel","It was a town in the south, in Simeon's land, called Bethul in Joshua 19:4 and Bethel in 1 Samuel 30:27. It is not the famous Bethel near Jerusalem, and it has no tie to the Aramean Bethuel.","place",1]],"v":[6325]},"H1301":{"l":"בָּרָק","x":"Bârâq","d":"Barak, an Israelite","p":"baw-rawk'","t":"baraq","g":"Barak","fb":[["barak","Barak","Judge living before Israel's Monarchy","He led Israel against Sisera, the Canaanite general, because Deborah told him to, and he would not go unless she came with him. That hesitation cost him the glory of the win.","person",13]],"v":[6605,6607,6608,6609,6611,6613,6613,6614,6615,6621,6624,6635,6638]},"H1303":{"l":"בַּרְקָן","x":"barqân","d":"a thorn (perhaps as burning brightly)","p":"bar-kwan'","t":"barqan","g":"briers","fb":[],"v":[6726,6735]},"H1319":{"l":"בָּשַׂר","x":"bâsar","d":"properly, to be fresh, i.e. full (rosy, figuratively cheerful); to announce (glad news)","p":"baw-sar'","t":"basar","g":"bear news","fb":[],"v":[7314,8018,8042,8130,8497,8498,8498,8504,8509,8759,10668,10843,14533,14910,15466,18428,18428,18477,18702,18702,18826,18843,19436,22698]},"H1361":{"l":"גָּבַהּ","x":"gâbahh","d":"to soar, i.e. be lofty; figuratively, to be haughty","p":"gaw-bah'","t":"gabahh","g":"it was haughty","fb":[],"v":[7441,11529,11748,11900,11922,12957,13724,13742,13860,15559,15817,16148,16891,16912,17722,17754,17792,18708,18748,18748,19280,20142,20811,20848,20891,20969,21158,21161,21173,21234,21239,21243,22513,22830]},"H1363":{"l":"גֹּבַהּ","x":"gôbahh","d":"elation, grandeur, arrogance","p":"go'-bah","t":"gobahh","g":"height","fb":[],"v":[7622,11233,11901,13115,13400,13873,14044,16857,20108,20481,20891,21239,21243,21518,21533,22387,22387]},"H1322":{"l":"בֹּשֶׁת","x":"bôsheth","d":"shame (the feeling and the condition, as well as its cause); by implication (specifically) an idol","p":"bo'-sheth","t":"bosheth","g":"shame","fb":[],"v":[7760,7760,11896,12244,13050,14435,14539,14585,14953,14973,15783,16168,18219,18221,18496,18726,18849,18990,19025,19026,19137,19238,19439,21994,21995,22217,22589,22757,22824,22838]},"H1308":{"l":"בְּשׂוֹר","x":"Bᵉsôwr","d":"Besor, a stream of Palestine","p":"bes-ore'","t":"besor","g":"Besor","fb":[["besor","Besor","","A brook in southern Judah. Two hundred of David's men were too worn out to cross it and stayed behind while the rest chased the Amalekite raiders. David then insisted that the men who stayed with the supplies share the spoil equally.","place",3]],"v":[7987,7988,7999]},"H1338":{"l":"בִּתְרוֹן","x":"Bithrôwn","d":"Bithron, a place East of the Jordan","p":"bith-rone'","t":"bithron","g":"Bitron","fb":[["bithron","Bithron","","Abner and his men marched through it by night on their way back to Mahanaim, after Asahel was killed chasing Abner. It was a district or ravine in the Jordan Valley on the east side of the river.","place",1]],"v":[8078]},"H1309":{"l":"בְּשׂוֹרָה","x":"bᵉsôwrâh","d":"glad tidings; by implication, reward for good news","p":"bes-o-raw'","t":"besorah","g":"news","fb":[],"v":[8130,8498,8500,8503,8505,9716]},"H1339":{"l":"בַּת־שֶׁבַע","x":"Bath-Shebaʻ","d":"Bath-Sheba, the mother of Solomon","p":"bath-sheh'-bah","t":"bath-sheba","g":"Bathsheba","fb":[["bath-sheba","Bath-sheba","David's wife living at the time of United Monarchy","She was Uriah the Hittite's wife. David saw her bathing, sent for her, and got her pregnant while Uriah was away fighting in David's own army. The cover-up ended with Uriah's death in battle, arranged by David.","person",11]],"v":[8262,8262,8310,8310,8728,8728,8732,8732,8733,8733,8745,8745,8748,8748,8783,8783,8788,8788,8789,8789,14691,14691]},"H1393":{"l":"גִּבְעֹנִי","x":"Gibʻônîy","d":"a Gibonite, or inhabitant of Gibon","p":"ghib-o-nee'","t":"giboni","g":"Gibeonites","fb":[["gibeonite","Gibeonite","","Saul broke the old treaty and killed some of them. Under David a famine followed, and it ended only when seven of Saul's descendants were handed over to the Gibeonites for execution.","place",7]],"v":[8581,8582,8582,8583,8584,8589,10723,12334]},"H1359":{"l":"גֹּב","x":"Gôb","d":"Gob, a place in Palestine","p":"gobe","t":"gob","g":"Gob","fb":[["gob","Gob","Gezer","Two fights with Philistine champions happened here. Sibbecai killed Saph, and Elhanan killed a brother of Goliath. Chronicles calls the place Gezer, and whether that is a copying difference or a nearby site is unclear.","place",2]],"v":[8598,8599]},"H1305":{"l":"בָּרַר","x":"bârar","d":"to clarify (i.e. brighten), examine, select","p":"baw-rar'","t":"barar","g":"[one who] purifies himself","fb":[],"v":[8629,8629,10575,10637,10861,12400,13652,14143,14143,17376,18637,18706,19037,20222,20932,22070,22090,22828]},"H1398":{"l":"גֶּבֶר","x":"Geber","d":"Geber, the name of two Israelites","p":"gheh'-ber","t":"geber","g":"Geber","fb":[["geber","Geber","Man living at the time of United Monarchy","Among Solomon's twelve district governors, each feeding the court for a month, two entries carry this name. The son of Geber was at Ramoth-gilead, and Geber son of Uri had Gilead itself, the old lands of Sihon and Og. Whether that is one man or two is unclear.","person",2]],"v":[8857,8863]},"H1356":{"l":"גֵּב","x":"gêb","d":"a log (as cut out); also well or cistern (as dug)","p":"gabe","t":"geb","g":"ditches","fb":[],"v":[8905,9592,9592,19295]},"H1324":{"l":"בַּת","x":"bath","d":"a bath or Hebrew measure (as a means of division) of liquids","p":"bath","t":"bath","g":"baths","fb":[],"v":[8960,8972,11221,11221,11251,17748,21639,21640,21640,21643,21643,21643,21643]},"H1377":{"l":"גְּבִירָה","x":"gᵉbîyrâh","d":"a mistress","p":"gheb-ee-raw'","t":"gebirah","g":"queen-mother","fb":[],"v":[9127,9262,9806,11506,19283,19636]},"H1340":{"l":"בַּת־שׁוּעַ","x":"Bath-Shûwaʻ","d":"Bath-shua,","p":"bath-shoo'-ah","t":"bath-shua","g":"Bathshua","fb":[["bath-shua","Bath-shua","David's wife living at the time of United Monarchy","Daughter of Shua. Chronicles uses the phrase for two different women, and here it names the Canaanite wife of Judah, the mother of Er, Onan and Shelah.","person",2]],"v":[10309,10309,10366,10366]},"H1388":{"l":"גִּבְעָא","x":"Gibʻâʼ","d":"Giba, a place in Palestine","p":"ghib-aw'","t":"giba","g":"of Gibea","fb":[["gibeah","Gibeah","Woman or town of the time of Divided Monarchy","Not Saul's Gibeah in Benjamin. This one is a Judahite settlement in 1 Chronicles 2:49, founded by a descendant of Caleb, and nothing more is recorded about it.","person",1]],"v":[10355]},"H1332":{"l":"בִּתְיָה","x":"Bithyâh","d":"Bithjah, an Egyptian woman","p":"bith-yaw'","t":"bithyah","g":"of Bithiah","fb":[["bithiah","Bithiah","Woman living at the time of Divided Monarchy","Pharaoh's daughter, married to Mered, a man of Judah. Her name means daughter of the LORD. That suggests she was seen as a convert to Israel's faith.","person",1]],"v":[10403]},"H1307":{"l":"בֵּרֹתִי","x":"Bêrôthîy","d":"a Berothite, or inhabitant of Berothai","p":"bay-ro-thee'","t":"berothi","g":"Beerothite","fb":[["berothite","Berothite","Beeroth","It tells you Naharai, Joab's armor-bearer and one of David's mighty men, came from Beeroth, a Gibeonite city allotted to Benjamin.","place",1]],"v":[10712]},"H1395":{"l":"גִּבְעָתִי","x":"Gibʻâthîy","d":"a Gibathite, or inhabitant of Gibath","p":"ghib-aw-thee'","t":"gibathi","g":"Gibeathite","fb":[["gibeathite","Gibeathite","Gibeah","Benjaminite archers and slingers from Gibeah, Saul's own town, who went over to David at Ziklag while he was still an outlaw.","place",1]],"v":[10722]},"H1302":{"l":"בַּרְקוֹס","x":"Barqôwç","d":"Barkos, one of the Nethimim","p":"bar-kose'","t":"barqoc","g":"of Barkos","fb":[["barkos","Barkos","Man living at the time of Exile and Return","His family were temple servants, Nethinim, who came back from Babylonian exile but could not prove their Israelite descent from the records.","person",2]],"v":[12080,12475]},"H1351":{"l":"גָּאַל","x":"gâʼal","d":"to soil or (figuratively) desecrate","p":"gaw-al'","t":"gaal","g":"they were defiled","fb":[],"v":[12089,12484,18802,18868,20433,21744,21744,22820,23095,23095,23100]},"H1312":{"l":"בִּשְׁלָם","x":"Bishlâm","d":"Bishlam, a Persian","p":"bish-lawm'","t":"bishlam","g":"Bishlam","fb":[["bishlam","Bishlam","Man living at the time of Exile and Return","A Persian official in Samaria. He joined in writing to King Artaxerxes against the rebuilding of Jerusalem's walls. Some scholars think the Aramaic word behind his name may not be a name at all.","person",1]],"v":[12117]},"H1325":{"l":"בַּת","x":"bath","d":null,"p":"bath","t":"bath","g":"baths","fb":[],"v":[12195,12195]},"H1373":{"l":"גַּבַּי","x":"Gabbay","d":"Gabbai, an Israelite","p":"gab-bah'ee","t":"gabbay","g":"Gabbai","fb":[["gabbai","Gabbai","Man living at the time of Exile and Return","Nehemiah's census of Jerusalem after the exile lists him as head of a family of Benjamin, and nothing else is recorded about him.","person",1]],"v":[12595]},"H1352":{"l":"גֹּאֶל","x":"gôʼel","d":"profanation","p":"go'-el","t":"goel","g":"the defilement(s)","fb":[],"v":[12699]},"H1385":{"l":"גְּבִנָה","x":"gᵉbinâh","d":"curdled milk","p":"gheb-ee-naw'","t":"gebinah","g":"cheese","fb":[],"v":[13095]},"H1378":{"l":"גָּבִישׁ","x":"gâbîysh","d":"crystal (from its resemblance to ice)","p":"gaw-beesh'","t":"gabish","g":"crystal","fb":[],"v":[13521]},"H1343":{"l":"גֵּאֶה","x":"gêʼeh","d":"lofty; figuratively, arrogant","p":"gay-eh'","t":"geeh","g":"proud [people]","fb":[],"v":[13874,13875,15432,16267,16831,16858,17696,20108]},"H1348":{"l":"גֵּאוּת","x":"gêʼûwth","d":"the same as H1346 (גַּאֲוָה)","p":"gay-ooth'","t":"geuth","g":"majesty","fb":[],"v":[14112,15334,15426,17846,17904,18139,18164,18166]},"H1386":{"l":"גַּבְנֹן","x":"gabnôn","d":"a hump or peak of hills","p":"gab-nohn'","t":"gabnon","g":"of peaks","fb":[],"v":[14914,14915]},"H1381":{"l":"גְּבָל","x":"Gᵉbâl","d":"Gebal, a region in Idumaea","p":"gheb-awl'","t":"gebal","g":"Gebal","fb":[["gebal","Gebal","","Byblos, to the Greeks, a Phoenician port north of Beirut. Ezekiel says its craftsmen caulked the ships of Tyre. The ruins gave up the Ahiram sarcophagus, carrying one of the earliest examples of the Phoenician alphabet.","place",2]],"v":[15247]},"H1362":{"l":"גָּבָהּ","x":"gâbâhh","d":"lofty (literally or figuratively)","p":"gaw-bawh'","t":"gabahh","g":"than a [person] haughty","fb":[],"v":[15517,16844,17436,21232]},"H1349":{"l":"גַּאֲיוֹן","x":"gaʼăyôwn","d":"haughty","p":"gah-ah-yone'","t":"gaayon","g":"arrogant people","fb":[],"v":[16101]},"H1344":{"l":"גֵּאָה","x":"gêʼâh","d":"arrogance","p":"gay-aw'","t":"geah","g":"pride","fb":[],"v":[16614]},"H1336":{"l":"בֶּתֶר","x":"Bether","d":"Bether, a (craggy) place in Palestine","p":"beh'-ther","t":"bether","g":"of ravine[s]","fb":[["bether","Bether","","The mountains of Bether, in a refrain of the Song of Solomon, are most likely rugged, cleft hills rather than one spot on a map.","place",1]],"v":[17570]},"H1337":{"l":"בַּת רַבִּים","x":"Bath Rabbîym","d":"the daughter (i.e. city) of Rabbah","p":"bath rab-beem'","t":"bath rabbim","g":"Bath-Rabbim","fb":[["bath-rabbim","Bath-rabbim","","A gate of Heshbon with pools near it, where the Song of Solomon finds the beloved's eyes: the fishpools in Heshbon by the gate of Bath-rabbim.","place",1]],"v":[17630,17630]},"H1365":{"l":"גַּבְהוּת","x":"gabhûwth","d":"pride","p":"gab-hooth'","t":"gabhuth","g":"of pride","fb":[],"v":[17695,17701]},"H1326":{"l":"בָּתָה","x":"bâthâh","d":"desolation","p":"baw-thaw'","t":"bathah","g":"a desolation","fb":[],"v":[17744]},"H1327":{"l":"בַּתָּה","x":"battâh","d":"desolation","p":"bat-taw'","t":"battah","g":"the cliffs","fb":[],"v":[17800]},"H1374":{"l":"גֵּבִים","x":"Gêbîym","d":"Gebim, a place in Palestine","p":"gay-beem'","t":"gebim","g":"Gebim","fb":[["gebim","Gebim","","A village just north of Jerusalem, and the name probably means cisterns. Isaiah pictures its people running as an invading army closes on the city.","place",1]],"v":[17880]},"H1341":{"l":"גֵּא","x":"gêʼ","d":"haughty","p":"gay'","t":"ge","g":"proud","fb":[],"v":[17974]},"H1360":{"l":"גֶּבֶא","x":"gebeʼ","d":"a reservoir; by analogy, a marsh","p":"geh'-beh","t":"gebe","g":"marshes","fb":[],"v":[18230,21689]},"H1357":{"l":"גֵּב","x":"gêb","d":"a locust (from its cutting)","p":"gabe","t":"geb","g":"of locusts","fb":[],"v":[18282]},"H1333":{"l":"בָּתַק","x":"bâthaq","d":"to cut in pieces","p":"baw-thak'","t":"bathaq","g":"to cut in pieces","fb":[],"v":[20801]},"H1380":{"l":"גְּבַל","x":"Gᵉbal","d":"Gebal, a place in Phoenicia","p":"gheb-al'","t":"gebal","g":"of Gebal","fb":[["gebal","Gebal","","Byblos, to the Greeks, a Phoenician port north of Beirut. Ezekiel says its craftsmen caulked the ships of Tyre. The ruins gave up the Ahiram sarcophagus, carrying one of the earliest examples of the Phoenician alphabet.","place",2]],"v":[21129]},"H1321":{"l":"בְּשַׁר","x":"bᵉshar","d":null,"p":"bes-ar'","t":"beshar","g":"flesh","fb":[],"v":[21768,21848,21937]},"H1370":{"l":"גְּבוּרָה","x":"gᵉbûwrâh","d":"power","p":"gheb-oo-raw'","t":"geburah","g":"(the)","fb":[],"v":[21777,21780]},"H1358":{"l":"גֹּב","x":"gôb","d":"a pit (for wild animals) (as cut out)","p":"gobe","t":"gob","g":"the den","fb":[],"v":[21911,21916,21920,21921,21923,21924,21927,21927,21928,21928]},"H1355":{"l":"גַּב","x":"gab","d":null,"p":"gab","t":"gab","g":"back","fb":[],"v":[21938]},"H1317":{"l":"בׇּשְׁנָה","x":"boshnâh","d":"shamefulness","p":"bosh-naw'","t":"boshnah","g":"shame","fb":[],"v":[22230]},"H1318":{"l":"בָּשַׁס","x":"bâshaç","d":"to trample down","p":"baw-shas'","t":"bashac","g":"trample","fb":[],"v":[22433]}}